GENUINE LAUNCH / REPEATABLE PROCEDURE
1. Use a fresh private run directory and disposable repository containing two
   fixture tasks. Strip inherited CODEX_*, CLAUDE_*, CLAUDECODE and ICQ_* context
   identifiers from the runner, retain normal installed user authentication,
   and set BBOXY_TEST_CUSTODY=memory. Never borrow another session identity.
2. Session::start(Config { binary, run_dir, repository, ... }) starts the app's
   own debug supervisor/logic. Send GuiAction::Spawn with harness_kind claude
   or codex, cwd=the disposable repository, location=local, fresh operation ID.
   Observe Spawned, ListSeats Running and native terminal content via Watch.
3. Resize to 120x40 and retain each returned View; ACK only reconstructed updates.
   Use Task::Delegate and Messaging::Send to the exact seats/SEAT/inbox sink.
4. Complete the installed client's normal native onboarding through the app's
   own GuiAction::Input. No --bare, trust bypass, manually supplied trusted_hash,
   external GUI events, osascript or desktop injection. Skip update advertisements.
5. If the stored DM does not wake the model, record that before entering a
   separate bracketed-paste operator prompt. Request orient, task_list,
   task_status, message_list, reply/ack, then task_report. Do not equate that
   operator prompt with native message delivery. Omit unrun verification/commit.
6. Independently query Messaging list/receipts and inspect the signed fixture
   task; do not accept only the model's final prose. Send a second unique DM
   after the turn ends, give no further input, and observe automatic wake.
7. Shut down through Session, confirm only recorded owned PIDs are gone, hash
   the evidence and remove the private completed build target.

